// one result is fully written, then a later result's writer accepts a prefix
// and returns an error. The run must fail at once, point at the idle
// declaration (physical line 7), identify the failing key and window range,
// and expose the writer's original error via errors.Is. The complete earlier
// results and the accepted prefix stay exactly as written (no undo, no
// completion, no resend); the rest of the batch and all later records are
// abandoned, and the still-open windows are not flushed at end of input.
