// and end 1200 key "b" alone. To produce end 1200 under slide 600 a window
// would need start 200, which is not a multiple of 600; so the second end is
// reached by an event whose [600,1600) window is *not* ready, while key "b"
// also has a [0,1000) window. The batch therefore is exactly:
//
//	{"a", [0,1000)}  {"k", [0,1000)}   (end 1000, keyed UTF-8: "a" < "k")
//	{"b", [200,1200)} is impossible at slide 600; see build below.
//
// To keep the alignment honest, the second end time is 1200 reached with
// window length 1000 over a start of 200 only when slide divides it; the
// fixture instead places "b" so it shares end 1000 as a *third* key and adds
// a distinct end 1600 that must NOT close, proving the watermark boundary.
// See idleBatchLines: the real ready batch (three results, two end times) is
